    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="74">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 74</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>CXVIII. Gif ðeowwealh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.19"/> Engliscne monnan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.20"/> ofslihð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.21"/>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sceal se ðe hine ah weorpan hine to honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.22"/> hlaforde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.23"/> ⁊ mægum oððe LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.24"/> scill. gesellan wið his feore.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.25"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>CXVIII. ............scne monnan ofslihð, þonne ..... ah weorpan hine to honda hlaforde ..... LX scill' gesellan w:ð his fe:re.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="120" ed="#liebermann"/>CXVIII. Gif þeowwealh Engliscne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.4"/> ofslihþ, ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sceal se þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.9"/> hine ah weorpan hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.9"/> to honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.4"/> hlaforde ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.4"/> magu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oþþe LX scll' gesyllan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.3"/> wið his feore.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.10-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="74" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe ðeowwalh frigne man ofslea. Gyf ðeowwealh Engliscne man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.2"/> ofslihð, ðonne sceal se ðe hine ah weorpan hine to handa hlaforde ⁊ magu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oððe syxtig scill' gesyllan wið his feore.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="74" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Si seruus Waliscus Anglicum hominem occidat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.10"/>, debet ille, cuius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.11"/> est, reddere eum domino (suo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.12"/>) et parentibus aut LX solid. dare pro uita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_74.lnote.oe.13"/> sua.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe ðeowwalh frigne man ofslea.] Gif ðeowwealh Engliscne monnan<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_74.attnote.fn.1"/> ofslihð, þonne sceal se ðe hine ah weorpan hine to honda hlaforde ⁊ mægum oððe LX scill. gesellan wið his feore.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="75" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="434" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CXVIII} Gif ðeowweahl Engliscne monnan ofslihð, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> sceal se ðe hine ah weorpan hine to honda hlaforde ⁊ mægum oððe LX sciƚƚ gesellan wið his feore.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_74.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="121" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein unfreier (Wälscher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_74.lnote.de.2"/>?) einen Englischen Mann erschlägt, dann soll<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_74.lnote.de.3"/> sein Eigenthümer ihn an [des Erschlagenen] Herrn und Verwandte ausliefern oder [ihnen] 60 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_74.lnote.de.4"/> für das Leben jenes [Sklaven] zahlen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If an unfree (Welsh?) man slays an Englishman, then his owner is to hand him over to the lord and kinsmen [of the slain man] or pay [them] 60 shillings for the life of that [slave].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="61" ed="#attenborough"/>If a Welsh slave slays an Englishman, his owner shall hand him over to the dead man's lord and kinsmen, or purchase his life for 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="407" ed="#whitelock"/>If a Welsh slave kills an Englishman, then he who owns him shall surrender him to the lord and kinsmen [of the slain man], or pay 60 shillings for his life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="435" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a Welsh slave kills an English man, then the owner shall turn him over to the [slain man’s] lord and kin or pay 60 shillings for his life.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="435"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_23-3">Ine 23.3</ref> <quote>§23 sets the value of a Welsh slave at "50 shillings, some 60."</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_27">Af 27</ref> <quote>he fleo ("let him flee") is unclear. Ine §75 states that if a Welsh slave kills an English man [...] Perhaps this is what the guilty party here is fleeing.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_23-3">Ine 23.3</ref> <quote>It is true that §75 requires the owner of a Welsh slave who has killed an Englishman to pay 60 shillings</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="290"><label>covered by</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_6">II Ew 6</ref> <quote>Penal slaves and the obligations of their kin (if any) had also been covered by Ine (n. 126)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-sanctuary" n="144"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Af_42-1">Af 42.1</ref> <quote>Chapter 74, for example, concerning what is to be done with a Welsh slave who commits homicide, furnishes the most obvious case; after being placed in the hands of those he has wronged, he is presumably not meant to survive. Yet the Alfredian clauses mentioned earlier are concerned neither with those already in servitude nor those reduced to penal slavery</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd. in</hi> mann</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. to mann</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-derit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-derit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. e. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. e. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt T Hn</hi> 70, 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in T Hn 70, 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">121</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wita <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wita MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þeofw. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> ðeowew. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þeofw. So; ðeowew. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-na <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-na So; man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ofslyhð <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ofslyhð So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">handa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">handa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rd ⁊ mag. <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> -rd ⁊ magan <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rd ⁊ mag. Ld; -rd ⁊ magan So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig s. gesyllan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig s. gesyllan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">120</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">feorh <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">feorh Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Teils aus Q, teils aus Or. wiederholt dies Hn 70, 5. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 33²; Berichtigung II 757 <hi rend="italic">u. o.</hi> S. 42 zur Rb</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 70, 5 repeats this, partly from Q, partly from Or. <hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 33²; correction II 757 <hi rend="italic">and above</hi> p. 42 on the Rb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Walliser 8. Über die Unfreien <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Girard <hi rend="italic">Actions noxales</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Nouv. rev. droit franç.</hi> XII 52. — Es fehlt ein Satz über Tötung eines Wallisers durch Walliser Sklaven: vermutlich entschied da Walliser Recht und Gericht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Walliser 8. On the unfree, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Girard <hi rend="italic">Actions noxales</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Nouv. rev. droit franç.</hi> XII 52. — A sentence on the killing of a Welshman by a Welsh slave is missing: presumably Welsh law and Welsh courts decided that case</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Unfreie (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 17 b) gilt also als Person. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Tierstrafe 2. a. — Herr <hi rend="spaced">und</hi> Verwandte des Erschlagenen bilden Einen Kreis, oder <hi rend="italic">and</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi> 2) heisst ‘beziehungsweise’, wie <hi rend="italic">mægas oððe hlaford</hi> VI As 1, 4; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Gefolge 22 b; Sippe 24. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The unfree man (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 17 b) is thus regarded as a person. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Tierstrafe 2. a. — The lord <hi rend="italic">and</hi> the kinsmen of the slain man form a single group, or else <hi rend="italic">and</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 2) means ‘or, as the case may be’, as in <hi rend="italic">mægas oððe hlaford</hi> VI As 1, 4; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Gefolge 22 b; Sippe 24. a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_74.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sklavenpreis; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Unfreie 7 a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Slave-price; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Unfreie 7 a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_74.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><label>monnan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mon</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">man</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
